@startuml
title SD01 - Calculate order discounts (AD05 / AD28)
autonumber

actor "Sales employee" as Sales
actor "Year-end system process" as YearEnd
participant "customer:Customer" as Customer
participant "discount:CustomerDiscount" as Discount
participant "order:Order" as Order

== Annual discount determination (AD28) ==
loop Each customer on 31 December
  YearEnd -> Customer: calculateAnnualRevenue()
  activate Customer
  note right of Customer
    Annual turnover is the amounts ACTUALLY PAID
    on fully paid invoices in the year ending on 31 December.
    Do not use gross order values or unpaid invoices.
  end note
  Customer --> YearEnd: annualRevenue
  deactivate Customer
  YearEnd -> Discount: determinePercentage(annualRevenue, nextYear)
  activate Discount
  note right of Discount
    < EUR 10,000: 5%
    >= EUR 10,000 and < EUR 20,000: 10%
    >= EUR 20,000: 15%
    Store this rate for the next calendar year (AD28).
  end note
  Discount --> YearEnd: computed rate (5%, 10% or 15%)
  YearEnd -> Discount: Store calendarYear = nextYear and percentage = computed rate
  Discount --> YearEnd: next-year rate recorded
  deactivate Discount
end

== Calculate a telephone order (AD05) ==
Sales -> Customer: checkOrderBlock()
activate Customer
Customer --> Sales: blocked or allowed
deactivate Customer
alt Blocked because debt collection is active
  note right of Sales: Reject new orders until the full outstanding balance is paid.
else Customer may order
  Sales -> Order: calculateTotalAmount()
  activate Order
  note right of Order
    Inputs: customer name, customer address and
    sum of ordered product prices (subtotal).
    No order is saved until the customer approves (AD05).
  end note
  Order -> Order: calculateOrderDiscount()
  note right of Order
    If subtotal >= EUR 500, subtract 5% of subtotal;
    otherwise order discount = EUR 0.
  end note
  alt First order and allowance not already applied on a previous order
    Order -> Order: calculateOneTimeDiscount()
    note right of Order
      Subtract 10% of the amount AFTER the order discount.
      The acquisition offer and ordinary first-order allowance
      are the SAME single 10% one-time discount (invoice field).
      oneTimeDiscountGranted = true means eligible, not consumed;
      On successful order approval/save, set the order's
      oneTimeDiscountApplied flag and do not apply it again.
    end note
  else Returning order or allowance already applied
    note right of Order: No one-time first-order discount.
  end
  Order -> Discount: Read stored customer rate for the order calendar year
  activate Discount
  Discount --> Order: customer discount percentage (5%, 10% or 15%)
  deactivate Discount
  Order -> Order: calculateCustomerDiscount()
  note right of Order
    Subtract customer discount from the amount remaining
    after the order discount and one-time discount.
  end note
  Order --> Sales: subtotal, order discount, one-time discount, customer discount, final total
  deactivate Order
end
@enduml
